## Evidence

Open work migrated from the canonical TODO. Add implementation and
validation evidence here as the task advances.

A corpus probe against the current lawful source installation narrowed the
`ui-images` semantic blocker class without relaxing its conversion policy. All
431 blocked packages contain one extracted `p3d-sprite` JSON member rather than
a physical raster, so the existing direct-texture gate is behaving correctly.

- 353 of the 431 package roots have a sibling source PNG beside the owning P3D.
- 308 of those PNGs exactly match the sprite-declared `image_size` dimensions.
- 45 sibling PNGs have different dimensions, and 78 packages have no sibling
  PNG, so neither group is eligible for automatic promotion from this evidence.
- The generated Pure3D contract declares `tlSpriteChunk` with one child
  `image` chunk, while the current extractor publishes only the sprite wrapper
  JSON.

The next implementation boundary is a verified raster-authority catalog, not a
planner heuristic. It must bind package identity, sprite evidence, raster path,
byte count, SHA-256, and dimensions before any matching package is promoted to
`Texture2D`; unmatched or dimension-conflicting packages must remain semantic
blockers.
